  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `node_content` is acceptable.\n\n- **Placement:** It sits on an explicit function with a body, which the built-in allows. It is a function-level exception for a body that never runs.\n- **Substance:** The commentary gives a real reason, not just difficulty. The test `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` asserts that the only recorded dependency is `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`. A content read would add an unwanted dependency, and the stub panics so that the guard fails if one happens.\n- **Agreement with the source:** `Graph::node_content` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs` is a required trait method, as the commentary says. The surrounding code matches the claim. `fingerprint` also panics, the renderer panics, and the test asserts exactly one record with only an outgoing-edge dependency. The test only passes if `node_content` is never reached, so the stated reason holds.\n- **No other gap:** The item has no other citations, so nothing is redundant or in the wrong role.",
